    {
      "id": "feedback-2",
      "title": "feedback 2 (brief)",
      "voiceover": {
        "text": "Its period matches Earth's spin, so it comes back to the same place in the sky each day. But its orbit's plane passes through Earth's centre and is tilted, so every day it swings north of the equator, then south. A fixed dish would lose it. The slip to avoid is thinking a twenty-four hour period is enough. The equatorial plane is the missing condition."
      },
